osure, ADD_CONTRACT→IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT completeness, final-step WIRE_UI all pass), and all 11 placeholders carry valid prefix/kind/language/declaring-project for the minter.\n- One structural decision worth noting: I verified in the tool source that the §9.6 registry check requires every referenced contract id to exist in the arc's `.contracts-json`, which only ever receives **this cycle's** minted ids — so `MODIFY_CONTRACT`/`MERGE_CONTRACT` on the pre-existing `MaterialProxy`/`SampleProxy` would fail handoff. The lifecycle re-shapes are therefore plain IMPLEMENT steps re-typing the registered contracts in place (the 0035 precedent), which also matches the operator's no-legacy/no-shim directive; the rationale is recorded in `.spec-md` §0.2 and the history row.\n- Interpretation calls recorded (in `.spec-md` and history): seeded samples stay `UserManaged` (only presets are `ProtectedBuiltIn`); the launcher carries Main-only between steps 4 and 45 so every intermediate state runs; scene vs experiment-collection persistence as two separate proxies; only the `Groups` collection type renames; the inverse terminal screen is named `SolverHandoffWindow`.\n\nBoth files are LF-clean, and the scans for lowercase normative keywords and stub/deferral phrasings came back empty.\nSpec 0038 is fully authored. Both spec files are written, validated, and the history row is appended.\n\n**What was produced:**\n\n- **`.spec-md`** — the steering narrative: binding constraints (elevate-every-primitive, no legacy/fallback/migration, no real IO beyond three named seams, FuncUI list hygiene, zero warnings, the condensed operator-UX checklist with the `.gitignore` collision check), the 11-placeholder contract table, and problem statements for Parts A–N.\n- **`.spec-jsonl`** — 47 forward-only steps covering the whole preliminary spec: the crash-fix hygiene sweep (Part A, CRITICAL, lands first), the workbench relocation + test-launcher executable, appsettings/app-scoped composition/`WindowLaun