{"at": "2026-07-10T19:05:06Z", "commit_ref": "441d564", "intent": "spec", "actor": "user", "kind": "input", "content": "The claim-check report flagged 1 item(s) that MUST be fixed before handoff. Apply the following edits to .spec-md:\n\n1. §0.2 -- REFUTED-NO-POINTER. The claim (Nothing library-related is serialized yet, so re-typed structures replace old ones cleanly and every app start re-seeds in memory.) is wrong; resolve per the claim-check report's evidence: Inferred assumption-shape ('yet' = current-state claim); no <file>:<symbol> pointer. Grep contradicts the flat reading: OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs:17-24 declares a 'Shareable material-library file format (§I.8 / R-4)' — module MaterialLibrary with a persisted-form MaterialEntryDto (:36) and schema-validated canonical-JSON export/import of `MaterialEntry list`; OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs also imports/exports MaterialEntry (importRefractiveIndexInfo :407, importCsv :432, exportCsv :459). The narrower reading does hold: the live composition re-seeds in memory (OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:129-147, createInMemory over builtInEntries/seedEntries) and neither OpticalConstructor.App nor OpticalConstructor.TestWindows references any library file IO. Spec-writer should anchor/qualify the sentence (e.g. no persisted library STATE; the §I.8 share/export format in Storage/Report.fs is metadata-only and unwired from the Main flow).\n\nMake NO other edits to .spec-md beyond the items above; every remaining claim in the report was CONFIRMED."}
{"at": "2026-07-10T19:05:06Z", "commit_ref": "441d564", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "output", "content": "Spec cycle (claim-check fix round): resolved the single REFUTED-NO-POINTER item in section 0.2 of .spec-md. The un-pointered current-state claim (\"Nothing library-related is serialized yet, so re-typed structures replace old ones cleanly and every app start re-seeds in memory\") was replaced by the anchored form: no library STATE is persisted -- the Main-flow composition builds every store in memory at startup (OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:129-147, createInMemory proxies over the Domain seeds) -- while the metadata-only library-file serialization that DOES exist is now named and scoped: the section I.8 share/export format (OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs:17-24, module MaterialLibrary, whose persisted MaterialEntryDto at :36 carries display metadata only) and the import/export helpers (OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs: importRefractiveIndexInfo :407, importCsv :432, exportCsv :459), both unwired from that composition, with section 0.3 already forbidding schema/import-export work this cycle. Every cited pointer was Read-verified against the tree before committing (spec 037 B-1). No other edits to .spec-md; .spec-jsonl unchanged."}
